    "body": "<!-- pr-reviewer: c1385b83e5c7fe50726115f71d0a30905c167d46 -->\n**Verdict: Ready for the maintainer to merge.**\n\nFull review at c1385b8, trial-merged with current main (clean, no conflicts).\n\n**What looks good**\n- The refusal is a machine-check problem (`judge::tap_gate`, crates/app/src/machine/judge.rs:194, called from `check_ops` in machine/mod.rs), so it runs for every post path that goes through the machine check. `check_ops` is reached from both `machine/mod.rs:155` and `posting_mounts.rs:126`. The pinning test goes through `posting::post_setup` on Tormach PathPilot, Fanuc and Haas, asserts the refusal names the op, the count and the machine, and asserts that no file is written.\n- No existing refusal is weakened. The change adds a gate and a stricter reader, and removes nothing.\n- A machine file without `rigid_tapping` (or with `null`) reads as \"not limited\". This is documented in docs/decisions/786-rigid-tapping.md and assets/machines/AGENTS.md, matches the existing unstated-limit law, and is pinned by the generic VMC test. Every shipped `.mch` still loads. A non-boolean value now refuses the file by name, both in the reader (post/src/machine/parse.rs) and in the Machines pane validator, instead of silently reading as unstated.\n- The message is plain English: \"N tap cycle(s) need rigid tapping, which <machine> cannot do - use a tapping head or thread milling\". The cycle is never converted to another cycle.\n- Tests live in the owning crate (app tests import app machine/posting code). Files stay under 400 lines (judge 203, mod 366, parse 387). There is a decision file, a Changelog line and `Fixes #786`. No snapshot PNG or golden changes. No new dependencies, and the diff touches no build.rs, `.github/` or scripts. No new command, so no new MCP tool is needed.\n\n**Local results (merged with main)**\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| app `rigid_tapping` | 5 passed |\n| app `machine` / `machine_library` / `machine_edit` | 33 / 11 / 12 passed |\n| app `posting` | 17 passed |\n| app `tormach_machines` / `tormach_post` / `tormach_routers` | 6 / 10 / 5 passed |\n| camcraft-post (all suites) | all passed |\n| ui lib `machines_pane` (CWD crates/ui) | 7 passed |\n| clippy `-p camcraft-post -p camcraft-app --all-targets -D warnings` | clean |\n\nI did not run camcraft-ui clippy separately (the UI change is test-only) and did not run the full batch tier.\n\n**Requested before merge**\nNone.\n\n**Notes (not blocking)**\n- A stated `false` only takes effect on machines whose file states it (the Tormach mills and routers). The Tormach lathes stay unstated (#795), as the PR says.\n- The \"Rigid tapping\" row wording on a real window was not hand-checked (the PR says so as well). The structural test covers the labels.\n\nA maintainer will approve and merge by hand.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
